at my wife runs  with a huge team of people from accounts  to all that type of stuff and then each  the way I do it is it's quite simple  each restaurant I open I have a chef  business partner yep so he's normally  one of my second-in-command I'm making  my partner me and my wife give him a  share of the business he then runs it as  his own we help secret the secret to the  success is what you know what seriously  hard work dedication be true to your  customers make sure that everybody who  walks with that door is treated like a  king and if you really care and a  passionate about what you do and don't  do it for like money or fame or anything  like that people get it you know and  they just come to your Russian because  they you know it's that I was just  cooking up clocked out overnight and  some guess that's about come up and  speak to and they were like you know  what you're doing such a great job here  and we love you  wine that's so great here it's still in  the kitchen and unusual for Somerset  lunch and dinner chef as I asked you to  sign this dish part of the ritual here  on the dish I'll ask you the question we  ask all visiting chefs judges if you  could share this meal with any person  past or present who would it be  I mean I'm so fortunate to have a very  supportive wife I don't see much or as  much as I'd like to so I know it's a  little bit cliche but I'd have to spend  it with my wife and my two beautiful  children who I miss dearly when I'm  traveling and stuff so that would that  would be you're gonna get points for  that cliche but it's a smart answer  yes very smart chef Jason Atherton thank  you
 

